  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1502.14 Disconnected impervious cover",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1502.14 “Disconnected impervious cover” means impervious cover that directs stormwater runoff to on-site pervious cover to infiltrate into the soil or be filtered by overland flow such that the stormwater does not contribute directly to runoff from a site, and such that the net rate and volume of stormwater runoff from the disconnected impervious cover is not greater than the rate and volume from undisturbed cover of equal area.\n\nSource. #9343, eff 1-1-09; ss by #12342, eff 8-15-17 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.14); ss by #14472, eff 1-19-26, EXPIRES: 1-19-36 (formerly Env-Wq 1502.16)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1500.html"
